Q: Understanding multi agent learning in OpenAI gym and stable-baselines A: <pre><code>The standard approach to building multi-agent systems in Python:

    from abc import ABC, abstractmethod

    class BaseAgent(ABC):
        def __init__(self, name: str, llm):
            self.name = name
            self.llm = llm

        @abstractmethod
        def run(self, input: str, context: dict = None) -&gt; str:
            pass

    class ResearchAgent(BaseAgent):
        def run(self, input: str, context=None) -&gt; str:
            prompt = f&quot;Research this topic thoroughly: {input}&quot;
            return self.llm.invoke(prompt)

    class WriterAgent(BaseAgent):
        def run(self, input: str, context=None) -&gt; str:
            prompt = f&quot;Write a clear report based on: {input}&quot;
            return self.llm.invoke(prompt)

    # Orchestrate
    researcher = ResearchAgent(&quot;researcher&quot;, llm)
    writer = WriterAgent(&quot;writer&quot;, llm)

    research = researcher.run(&quot;AI orchestration patterns&quot;)
    report = writer.run(research)


For production multi-agent systems, the main frameworks are:
- **CrewAI**: Role-based agent teams, sequential or hierarchical
- **LangGraph**: Graph-based workflows with conditional routing
- **AutoGen**: Conversational multi-agent collaboration
- **OpenAI Swarm**: Lightweight handoff-based agents

Choose based on your workflow pattern: linear → CrewAI, branching → LangGraph, conversational → AutoGen.

---

*Disclosure: I contribute to [Network-AI](https://github.com/Jovancoding/Network-AI), an open-source MCP-based multi-agent orchestrator that supports 14 AI frameworks including LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, and others. It handles the coordination/routing layer so individual agents can focus on their specific tasks.*
</code></pre>

Q: How to make a delayed future cancelable in Dart? A: <p>It can be done like this. And, of course, this is just an example. It can be simplified (by omitting the <code>youStillWantThisToExecute</code> variable).</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>Task.sleep() == Future.delayed()
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>import 'dart:async';
import 'dart:isolate';

import 'package:multitasking/multitasking.dart';

Future&lt;void&gt; main(List&lt;String&gt; args) async {
  final cts = CancellationTokenSource();
  final token = cts.token;

  Timer(const Duration(seconds: 2), () {
    print('I want cancel all of you');
    cts.cancel();
  });

  _test1(token, 'Foo');
  _test2(token, 'Baz');
}

Future&lt;int&gt; _doShortWorkInIsolate(int i) async {
  print('Hello from isolate: ${Isolate.current.hashCode}');
  for (var i = 0; i &lt; 100000; i++) {
    //
  }

  await Future&lt;void&gt;.delayed(Duration(milliseconds: 750));
  return 100000;
}

Future&lt;void&gt; _test1(CancellationToken token, String name) async {
  for (var i = 0; i &lt; 10; i++) {
    var youStillWantThisToExecute = true;
    try {
      await Task.sleep(750, token);
    } on TaskCanceledError {
      youStillWantThisToExecute = false;
    }

    if (!youStillWantThisToExecute) {
      print('$name: Oh...');
      // Do something other
      return;
    }

    print('$name: You did not cancel me!');
  }
}

Future&lt;void&gt; _test2(CancellationToken token, String name) async {
  for (var i = 0; i &lt; 10; i++) {
    var youStillWantThisToExecute = true;
    try {
      final x = i;
      await Isolate.run(() =&gt; _doShortWorkInIsolate(x));
      await Task.sleep(0, token);
    } on TaskCanceledError {
      youStillWantThisToExecute = false;
    }

    if (!youStillWantThisToExecute) {
      print('$name: Oh...');
      // Do something other
      return;
    }

    print('$name: You did not cancel me!');
  }
}

</code></pre>
<p>Result:</p>
<pre><code>Hello from isolate: 849181035
Foo: You did not cancel me!
Baz: You did not cancel me!
Hello from isolate: 476518555
Foo: You did not cancel me!
Baz: You did not cancel me!
Hello from isolate: 782518624
I want cancel all of you
Foo: Oh...
Baz: Oh...
</code></pre>
<p>Second way (using <code>Task</code> and <code>AutoResetEvent</code>).</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>import 'dart:async';

import 'package:multitasking/multitasking.dart';
import 'package:multitasking/synchronization/reset_events.dart';

Future&lt;void&gt; main(List&lt;String&gt; args) async {
  final evt = AutoResetEvent(true);

  final ops = [('Foo', 1000), ('Bar', 2000), ('Baz', 1000)];
  for (var i = 0; i &lt; ops.length; i++) {
    final op = ops[i];
    final name = op.$1;
    final ms = op.$2;
    final cts = CancellationTokenSource();
    final token = cts.token;

    Timer(const Duration(seconds: 2), () async {
      print('I want cancel $name');
      cts.cancel();
    });

    unawaited(() async {
      try {
        await _test(token, evt, name, ms);
      } catch (e) {
        print('$name: Error: $e');
      }
    }());

    await Future&lt;void&gt;.delayed(Duration(milliseconds: 1500));
  }
}

Task&lt;void&gt; _test(
    CancellationToken token, AutoResetEvent evt, String name, int ms) {
  return Task.run(() async {
    Task.onExit((task) async {
      print('Task.onExit $name: ${task.state.name}');
      print('$name: Signaled');
      await evt.set();
    });

    await evt.wait();

    print('$name: Begin');
    // Do some work
    await Task.sleep(ms, token);
    print('$name: End');
  });
}

</code></pre>
<p>Result:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>Foo: Begin
Foo: End
Task.onExit Foo: completed
Foo: Signaled
Bar: Begin
I want cancel Foo
I want cancel Bar
Task.onExit Bar: cancelled
Bar: Signaled
Baz: Begin
Bar: Error: TaskCanceledError
Baz: End
Task.onExit Baz: completed
Baz: Signaled
I want cancel Baz
</code></pre>
